# Release configuration for `pnpm run build` (Vite mode "production").
#
# Deliberately blank, and committed on purpose. Vite resolves env files in the order
#
#   .env  <  .env.local  <  .env.production  <  .env.production.local
#
# and applies the process environment last of all. This file therefore stops a
# developer's `.env.local` from silently deciding the backend address of a deployable
# bundle — which is exactly how the previous release candidate shipped with
# http://localhost:8080 compiled into dist/.
#
# `VITE_API_BASE_URL` is inlined at build time, so it must be supplied when the release
# is built, not when it is deployed:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://engine.example.com pnpm run build
#
# Use `VITE_API_BASE_URL=/` when the dashboard is served from the engine's own origin
# behind a single reverse proxy. vite.config.ts fails the build when neither is given,
# so an unconfigured release cannot be produced by accident.
#
# Do not hard-code a deployment URL below unless every deployment of this repository
# shares it. Whatever is written here ends up in the artifact for everyone.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
